    not_duplicate_of: []  # ee82
    pr_ref:  # ee82
    description: "Follow-up to WI-vurop. WI-banaf + WI-vurop covered bare-name imports and member calls on namespace/default imports. Remaining gap: bare global identifiers used without an explicit import — common in browser-heavy projects.\n\nExamples:\n- console.log(), console.error()\n- localStorage.getItem(), sessionStorage.setItem()\n- navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition()\n- document.querySelector(), window.fetch()\n- WebSocket.send() (constructed via `new WebSocket(...)`)\n\nApproach: catalog-driven. Consume the existing io-boundaries catalog's modules entry (logging, storage, net_send, etc.) and emit unresolved-call edges for known global object.method patterns where `object` is in a known-globals list and no import binding shadows it.\n\nREGRESSION TEST: a TypeScript file with `console.log(x); localStorage.setItem(\"k\",\"v\")` and no imports must produce one logging boundary and one storage_write boundary.\n\nPer human request on WI-vurop discussion 2026-04-14T19:04:02Z."  # ee82
    fields: {}  # ee82
